<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell 16 points to 1,294.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell 16 points to 1,294.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for</p>
<p>spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,294 today from</p>
<p>1,310 on July 25, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals</p>
<p>1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates</p>
<p>in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1411    12.806	  1420    12.894</p>
<p>   1a   1286  9738.000	  1295  9806.000</p>
<p>   2    1566    22.375	  1588    22.688</p>
<p>   2a   1529 12538.000	  1552 12731.000</p>
<p>   3    1424    13.138	  1458    13.450</p>
<p>   3a   1147  9050.000	  1185  9350.000</p>
<p>   6    1276    13.156	  1279    13.188</p>
<p>   7    1166     5.675	  1167     5.681</p>
<p>   8     844     9.281	   845     9.294</p>
<p>   9     708  6188.000	   725  6344.000</p>
<p>  10    1132     5.719	  1133     5.721</p>
